{
  "format": "wspradar.config",
  "schema_version": 1,
  "profile": {
    "id": "griffiths_squibb_rx_performance",
    "title": {
      "en": "Prof. Griffiths (G3ZIL) RX Performance: A Month on 40 m with a Low Dipole"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "[Publication: Griffiths, G., & Squibb, N. J. (2017). Improving HF band SNR from analysis of WSPR spots](https://www.researchgate.net/publication/319903566_Improving_HF_Band_SNR_from_analysis_of_WSPR_spots)\n\nA Performance-only re-analysis of G3ZIL’s 40 m WSPR reception throughout April 2017. Instead of comparing G3ZIL with G4HZX, it asks where, when and how consistently the G3ZIL low-dipole station decoded transmitters that were independently confirmed active elsewhere. The month provides more than 600,000 confirmed opportunities from nearly 2,000 transmitting stations, exposing geographic reach, distance-dependent Decode Rate, successful Target SNR and pronounced UTC-hour structure. EA4URA (IN80CI) is preselected to show how the population-level evidence resolves into one specific radio path, with 9,499 confirmed opportunities and a clear diurnal reception profile. This is whole-station RX Performance evidence; it does not by itself isolate antenna gain or establish the drying-soil effect discussed in the paper."
    }
  },
  "settings": {
    "core_parameters": {
      "analysis_direction": "rx",
      "callsign": "G3ZIL",
      "qth": "IO90HW",
      "band": "40m",
      "time_selection": {
        "start_utc": "2017-04-01T00:00Z",
        "end_utc": "2017-05-01T00:00Z"
      }
    },
    "comparison_parameters": {
      "mode": "none"
    },
    "advanced_parameters": {
      "solar_state": "all",
